    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T04:26:36Z",
    "body": "PR #3219 preserves the nominal line and arc perimeter. It checks clearance around the specified start hole before and after coordinate rounding.\n\nThe inspection export leaves the entry move to the control. A straight line from the start to the selected seam can clear the perimeter even when it meets the seam at an oblique angle. That check alone cannot establish the path the control uses or the clearance along that path.\n\nFor a cutting setup, the remaining checks include the actual entry and join, pass offsets for the installed 10 mm process, physical stock and Z, and the specified slug restraint and separation. The zero-step preview leaves these items open. Issue #3179 tracks verification of the physical setup and process.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
